data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":86,"item_id":"rs_060b1141c313160a016acb4ea6d3c887d2a9ab5a93fcb747f0","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating file testing strategy**\n\nI’m considering whether I have enough time to test the new append feature by writing a new file. I think I can use existing helpers to add tests by editing and inserting before what already exists. I'm also thinking about migrating legacy schema tasks and how they position nonstandard entries. It might make sense to focus on the single test seed tasks, move two out, create a new source, and return reversed assertions."}

